            0.908,
            0.172
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Why is the speed of light denoted by ‘c’?"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.69,
            0.173,
            0.93,
            0.392
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Scientific symbols often come from history, and are based on international agreements, not necessarily abbreviations of convenience. For example, the speed of light, is usually denoted with the symbol c, since it comes from the Latin word celeritas, meaning speed. Today, the speed of light is one of the physical constants, defined to be exactly 299792458 m/s."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
