            0.611
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Threads of Curiosity"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.147,
            0.629,
            0.468,
            0.646
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Why is a kilogram used everywhere?"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.145,
            0.649,
            0.61,
            0.759
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "When we buy rice or vegetables we expect a kilogram to mean the same amount everywhere (Fig. 1.1). Imagine the confusion if we used different weights everywhere! Thankfully, measurements are based on agreed international standards, not local objects or opinions. Standard units allow scientific results to be compared, and ensure fairness in daily life and trade."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
